1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,495
Study Companion — a source-grounded, adaptive AI tutor

2
00:00:08,495 --> 00:00:18,689
Built for the Multimodal AI Hackathon 2026, Track D:
Personalized Tutoring & Adaptive Learning

3
00:00:18,689 --> 00:00:28,883
The problem: study material is scattered across lecture videos,
textbooks and slides — and generic chatbots answer from anywhere
but your course.

4
00:00:28,883 --> 00:00:39,077
Study Companion ingests your own material — PDF, slides, notes,
and timestamped lecture transcripts — with zero manual preprocessing.

5
00:00:39,077 --> 00:00:50,971
Every passage keeps its exact origin: page number, slide number,
or video timestamp. That is the foundation for source grounding.

6
00:00:50,971 --> 00:01:02,864
Uploading three formats now: a textbook-style notes file,
a lecture slide deck, and a lecture transcript.

7
00:01:02,864 --> 00:01:14,757
Each file is parsed into source-linked content units:
13 passages from 3 files, in a couple of seconds.

8
00:01:14,757 --> 00:01:28,349
One click builds the course map: topics, subtopics, key concepts
and prerequisites — with every unit tagged to its topic.

9
00:01:28,349 --> 00:01:41,942
The tutor answers strictly from your material.
Every claim carries a citation to the exact unit.

10
00:01:41,942 --> 00:01:55,534
Ask about the learning rate — the answer cites the notes passage
and the slide where the update rule is defined.

11
00:01:55,534 --> 00:02:07,427
Click a citation and the exact source excerpt opens.
No black boxes — the student can verify everything.

12
00:02:07,427 --> 00:02:19,320
Now an off-material question: the capital of France is nowhere
in the material. The tutor declines instead of hallucinating.

13
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:31,214
The refusal is explicit and flagged in the UI — outside knowledge
is never blended silently with course content.

14
00:02:31,214 --> 00:02:43,107
Adaptive assessment: pick a topic, count and difficulty.
Questions are generated from the tagged units.

15
00:02:43,107 --> 00:02:55,000
Every question is independently verified: a second LLM pass solves
it from the source excerpt. Mismatches are dropped or repaired.

16
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:06,893
Each question is tagged to a topic, a difficulty and a source unit —
and repeated questions are blocked across assessments.

17
00:03:06,893 --> 00:03:18,787
Answer a question and get cited feedback plus the model answer.
The learner model updates immediately.

18
00:03:18,787 --> 00:03:30,680
Mastery is estimated with Bayesian Knowledge Tracing per topic,
with question-type aware guess and slip priors.

19
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:42,573
The dashboard shows per-topic mastery and weak topics —
the signal the tutor and recommendations adapt to.

20
00:03:42,573 --> 00:03:54,466
And a 7-day study plan weighted by mastery and forgetting curves —
so review time goes where it matters.

21
00:03:54,466 --> 00:04:06,360
The evaluation suite measures retrieval hit-rate and MRR,
faithfulness, answer relevancy and refusal accuracy

22
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:18,253
on a labeled test set — plus simulated student profiles
that report mastery gains and repetition rate.

23
00:04:18,253 --> 00:04:30,146
Everything runs locally on any OpenAI-compatible model.
Code, docs and evaluation results are in the public repo.

24
00:04:30,146 --> 00:04:42,040
Study Companion — tutoring that stays grounded in your course.
github.com/maebahesioru/multimodal-study-companion
